    Limit the number of results of External API events/series list endpoints (#8180)
    
    Fixes #3536
    
    A request to /api/events without a limit tried to load all events at
    once, which fails with a server error for installations with a large
    number of events.
    
    This adds a hard cap to events (and series), so any requests that try to
    set the limit over 10.000 now get a 400.
    If no limit is specified, the events endpoint now behaves the same as
    the series endpoint and sets limit to 100.
    The 10.000 is very much a magic number and should maybe be lower?
    
    Adds a new API version cause this is technically a breaking change.
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    Test the API with all kinds of limits, ideally with an Opencast with
    over 10.000 events.
    
